NAME: Nightly vault backup
OWNER: Chief
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every day at 1:15 AM (Eastern)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Chris says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/cog-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Nightly vault backup" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time ET> · Nightly vault backup · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/cog-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Chris only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/cog-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/cog-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time ET> · Nightly vault backup · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, append "<time ET> · Nightly vault backup · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time ET> · Nightly vault backup · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/cog-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Copy every note in /workspace/cog-team/vault/ that changed since the last backup to the Google Drive folder "GrokBot Vault", keeping the same folder paths, so Chris can open it in Obsidian. Write the list of files to this month's log. Never delete anything in Drive. Send Chris nothing unless the backup failed two nights in a row.
